7592186045443 true] [17592186483545 1083 #uuid "5b96278e-eb56-5e2c-8b74-597a29b2b2a0" 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483546 1080 "\\frac{3}{2(5-3x)^{2}}+C" 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483546 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483546 1083 #uuid "6a17550f-8b1e-5076-b4f3-14f620872486" 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483547 1080 "\\frac{2}{(3-x)^{4}}+C" 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483547 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483547 1083 #uuid "a0336689-0e13-5f83-9272-b3409590e5d2" 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483548 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483551 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483548 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483548 1071 "$\\int \\frac{3}{(5-3x)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483548 1072 #uuid "b8425667-976e-5474-9182-8785229638c8" 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483548 1074 "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 3(5-3x)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=5-3x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3(5-3x)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int {u}^{-3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\int {u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int {u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(-2)}{u}^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(5-3x)^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(5-3x)^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{2(5-3x)^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(5-3x)^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(5-3x)^{-2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)(5-3x)^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5-3x)+0 \\\\  & =-(5-3x)^{-3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =3(5-3x)^{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(5-3x)^{3}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483549 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483553 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483549 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483549 1071 "$\\int \\frac{4}{(3-x)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483549 1072 #uuid "beed05dd-1df0-5509-b310-7367b8962226" 13194139535233 17592186045443 true] [17592186483549 1074 "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 4(3-x)^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3-x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4(3-x)^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int {u}^{-5}\\cdot (-1)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)\\int {u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\int {u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{(-4)}{u}^{-4}+C \\\\  & =(3-x)^{-4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(3-x)^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(3-x)^{4}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(3-x)^{4}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(3-x)^{-4}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =(-4)(3-x)^{-5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3-x)+0 \\\\  & =(-4)(3-x)^{-5}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4(3-x)^{-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(3-x)^{5}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 1319413953523